# The build stage does `COPY . .`, so anything listed here never reaches the
# image. Two reasons it matters:
#
#   .env holds real secrets. Baking one into an image ships those secrets to
#   wherever the image goes, and nothing in the app would ever tell you.
#
#   node_modules, .next and generated/ are rebuilt inside the image against
#   its own platform. Copying a host build in makes the image both slower to
#   build and wrong - native modules compiled for the host do not run there.
.env
.env.*
node_modules
.next
/generated
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

.git
.github
backups
*.md
!README.md
